"tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/red/v1/referencia/upstream#consultar-tnet-sin-confundir-apis","content":"La documentación y ejemplos históricos de TNet pueden utilizar nombres que ya no existen en Eco. Cuando sea necesario consultar upstream, primero hay que traducir el concepto mediante la tabla de equivalencias de Eco."},"600":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/runtime/cliente","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/runtime/cliente","type":"page","content":"Cliente","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Red","Red","Contenido","Runtime"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/red/v1/runtime/cliente"},"601":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/runtime/cliente-0","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/runtime/cliente","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/red/v1/runtime/cliente","content":"Ciclo de vida del cliente de Eco, conexión, transporte y gestión de la sesión."},"602":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/runtime/cliente-1","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/runtime/cliente","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/red/v1/runtime/cliente#cliente","content":"Cliente"},"603":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/runtime/cliente-2","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/runtime/cliente","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/red/v1/runtime/cliente#flujo","content":"Flujo"},"604":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/runtime/cliente-3","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/runtime/cliente","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/red/v1/runtime/cliente#estados","content":"Estados"},"605":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/runtime/cliente-4","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/runtime/cliente","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/red/v1/runtime/cliente#conexión","content":"Conexión"},"606":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/runtime/cliente-5","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/runtime/cliente","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/red/v1/runtime/cliente#procesamiento","content":"Procesamiento"},"607":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/runtime/cliente-6","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/runtime/cliente","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/red/v1/runtime/cliente#canales","content":"Canales"},"608":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/runtime/cliente-7","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/runtime/cliente","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/red/v1/runtime/cliente#jugador-local","content":"Jugador local"},"609":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/runtime/cliente-8","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/runtime/cliente","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/red/v1/runtime/cliente#servidor-local","content":"Servidor local"},"610":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/runtime/cliente-9","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/runtime/cliente","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/red/v1/runtime/cliente#referencia-a-tnet","content":"Referencia a TNet"},"611":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/runtime/cliente-10","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/runtime/cliente","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/red/v1/runtime/cliente#cliente","content":"El cliente mantiene la conexión, procesa paquetes y conserva el estado local de la sesión."},"612":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/runtime/cliente-11","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/runtime/cliente","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/red/v1/runtime/cliente#cliente","content":"> El uso habitual de Eco se apoya en su API pública; `ClienteJuego` contiene gran parte de la implementación interna."},"613":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/runtime/cliente-12","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/runtime/cliente","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/red/v1/runtime/cliente#estados","content":"`isConnected`, `isTryingToConnect`, `isJoiningChannel`, `isInChannel` y `stage` representan estados distintos de la sesión. Eco mantiene además colecciones separadas de canales activos y de uniones pendientes."},"614":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/runtime/cliente-13","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/runtime/cliente","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/red/v1/runtime/cliente#conexión","content":"TCP es el transporte principal. Eco puede utilizar UDP cuando está disponible y admite una conexión personalizada mediante `IConnection`."},"615":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/runtime/cliente-14","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/runtime/cliente","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/red/v1/runtime/cliente#procesamiento","content":"Los paquetes entrantes se procesan identificando su `Paquete` y ejecutando la operación correspondiente. El cliente también mantiene estadísticas de bytes y paquetes y puede limitar el tiempo de procesamiento por frame."},"616":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/runtime/cliente-15","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/runtime/cliente","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/red/v1/runtime/cliente#canales","content":"El cliente puede participar en varios canales simultáneamente. `JoinChannel`, `LeaveChannel`, `LeaveAllChannels`, `IsInChannel`, `IsJoiningChannel` y `GetChannel` gestionan esta pertenencia."},"617":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/runtime/cliente-16","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/runtime/cliente","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/red/v1/runtime/cliente#jugador-local","content":"El cliente expone `playerID`, `playerName`, `playerData`, `serverTime`, `serverUptime` y el acceso a sus canales."},"618":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/runtime/cliente-17","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/runtime/cliente","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/red/v1/runtime/cliente#servidor-local","content":"Eco puede conectar un `ClienteJuego` directamente con un `ServidorJuego` dentro del mismo proceso, evitando sockets pero conservando el flujo lógico cliente-servidor."},"619":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/runtime/cliente-18","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/runtime/cliente","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/red/v1/runtime/cliente#referencia-a-tnet","content":"Eco"},"620":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/runtime/cliente-19","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/runtime/cliente","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/red/v1/runtime/cliente#referencia-a-tnet","content":"TNet"},"621":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/runtime/cliente-20","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/runtime/cliente","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/red/v1/runtime/cliente#referencia-a-tnet","content":"`ClienteJuego`"},"622":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/runtime/cliente-21","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/runtime/cliente","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/red/v1/runtime/cliente#referencia-a-tnet","content":"`GameClient`"},"623":{"id":"/docs/red/v1/runtime/cliente-22","page_id":"/docs/red/v1/runtime/cliente","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/red/v1/runtime/cliente#referencia-a-tnet","